# satpulsewb with no -L: the real default-port path (the canonical port, or an
# OS-picked fallback when it is taken), an all-interfaces bind, and a generated
# access token -- the URL and token the runner parses from stdout. -d
# auto-connects at startup over the read-only FIFO the runner allocated, so the
# session skips probing, falls to passive detection, and still reaches connected.
-d
${SATPULSE_TEST_SERIAL}
